                                "sense_id": "06ba6a2d-66dd-3176-91c4-62fdbcb339b7",
                                "text": "TUAPHOLL. A term used by the Druids to designate an unhallowed circumambulation around the sacred cairn, or altar, the movement being against the sun, that is, from west to east by the north, the cairn being on the left hand of the circumambulator."
